ayed's US Senate campaign now? This is too much! El-Sayed courted Michigan Muslim centers for votes -- and these centers are where clerics portrayed the U.S. as Satan, and sought \u2018revenge\u2019 on Zionists. ", "last_comment_created": 1793369045379, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 15, "score_up": 179, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "Newly surfaced recordings show the Democratic candidate courting votes at tax-exempt Islamic centers, where clergy and Islamic scholars called America the \"House of [Satan],\" asked Allah to support the fight against Israel, and prayed for vengeance against Zionists and their backers.", "large_image": "ojWh0rHrjX8wms5R.png", "title": "El-Sayed courted Muslim centers where clerics portrayed U.S as Satan, sought \u2018revenge\u2019 on Zionists"}, "post_flair_text": "SAVE AMERICA", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToUFkGLV", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 35, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8912215, "raw_content": "Privacy International immediately called for a boycott of Intel products, arguing the PSN would let websites track and profile users without consent. That's laughable now.\n\nWe were concerned then where things were going, but the industry got it's way in the end anyway. We learned to never just blindly trust anyhing they did, because everytime there was a hidden agenda or alternate motivation behind everything...EVERYTIME!\" Not just sometimes.\n\nRighteous indignant paranoia was instill into all of us then, and we all had vigorous discussions at bars or on BBS's on where society was heading. Well we're there. You missed out. All you know is what they want you to know and feel!\n\nIt's all too late now, but old habits never die. It doesn't matter now anyway right? Lemmings was the best video game back then. Describes exactly where everything went.", "author": "Spunas1", "created": 1793354473009, "profile_picture": "M9kBvo0NRYhC", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "I_Love_45-70_Gov", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Remember the game Lemmings? How prophetic!I've been around it since the 286 12mhz days. 1985. Watched the entire industry change and grow, and was around when they backdoored Processor Serial Number (PSN).", "last_comment_created": 1793368821488, "content": "<p>Privacy International immediately called for a boycott of Intel products, arguing the PSN would let websites track and profile users without consent. That's laughable now.</p>\n<p>We were concerned then where things were going, but the industry got it's way in the end anyway. We learned to never just blindly trust anyhing they did, because everytime there was a hidden agenda or alternate motivation behind everything...EVERYTIME!&quot; Not just sometimes.</p>\n<p>Righteous indignant paranoia was instill into all of us then, and we all had vigorous discussions at bars or on BBS's on where society was heading. Well we're there. You missed out. All you know is what they want you to know and feel!</p>\n<p>It's all too late now, but old habits never die. It doesn't matter now anyway right? Lemmings was the best video game back then. Describes exactly where everything went.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 19, "score_up": 35, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "li